Short:        Smart File System handler for 68020+
Author:       Ilkka Lehtoranta
Uploader:     ilkleht gmail com (Ilkka Lehtoranta)
Type:         disk/misc
Version:      1.0
Architecture: m68k-amigaos
Requires:     AmigaOS 2.04+, 68020+, existing SFS0 volume
URL:          https://github.com/ilehtoranta/CopperSFS
Distribution: Aminet

CopperSFS 1.0 is an experimental AmigaDOS filesystem handler for classic
Smart File System (SFS\0) volumes. It is an independent implementation of
the filesystem originally developed by John Hendrikx.

This package contains the filesystem handler and documentation, without
additional filesystem tools. Install CopperSFS as L:CopperSFS on a
separate boot volume.

This package requires a 68020 or newer CPU. Every included executable uses
the 68020 instruction set. Use disposable test volumes with independent
backups. Physical devices and other ROM configurations remain unqualified.

The default handler uses buffered writes and a 256 KiB clean-data cache.
Recent unflushed changes may be lost after a crash. The optional strict
handler commits each successful mutation before replying. Both modes use
the same recovery journal and ordered flush barriers. Recover interrupted
CSUN transactions with CopperSFS before using another filesystem handler.

Cache capacity is selected by executable, not by a mount flag:
  CopperSFS                 buffered, 256 KiB (default)
  CopperSFS-strict          strict,   256 KiB
  Variants/CopperSFS-cache0   buffered, disabled
  Variants/CopperSFS-cache128 buffered, 128 KiB
  Variants/CopperSFS-cache512 buffered, 512 KiB
  Variants/CopperSFS-cache2048 buffered, 2 MiB requested

The pool falls back to smaller allocations or uncached reads when needed.
ADDBUFFERS controls a different cache. Default loaded-and-mounted memory
measured about 570 KiB on the test profile; INSTALL.txt gives full figures.

The underlying default and strict code was A/B tested against the 68k
SmartFilesystem 1.279 from Joerg Strohmayer's development branch under
Kickstart 3.1, including concurrent reads/writes, independent disk checks
and 329 interrupted-write/recovery cases across
both implementations. Version stamping preserves all original code/data
and relocations. These new binary hashes have not received a new full A/B
sweep. The 1.0 default passed native Version 40.3 identification/date and
mount/read checks. Alternate cache builds have narrower qualification.
Read VALIDATION.txt for the exact coverage and crash-model limits.

Read INSTALL.txt before installing or changing the selected executable.
Verify files against SHA256SUMS.txt on a host with SHA-256 support.
CopperSFS is distributed under the MIT license in LICENSE.txt.
Native handler integration source is not included.

Report reproducible problems at the public repository, including handler
hash, CPU, OS, device, geometry and steps using a disposable volume.
